# Design System Rules for CFGY Project

## Overview

This document provides comprehensive rules for integrating Figma designs into the CFGY codebase using the Model Context Protocol. The project uses React with TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, and follows a component-based architecture.

## 1. Design Token Definitions

### Location
Design tokens are defined in two places:
- **Primary**: `web/tailwind.config.js` - Tailwind configuration with theme extensions
- **Utilities**: `web/src/index.css` - Additional utility classes via `@layer utilities`

### Color Tokens

Colors follow a semantic naming convention:

```javascript
// From tailwind.config.js
colors: {
  text: {
    dark: '#000033',
    light: '#FFFFFF',
  },
  basic: {
    'brand-color': '#0F0F7B',
    gray: '#949494',
    secondary: '#EBF1FF',
    accent: '#3333CC',
  },
  states: {
    error: '#D70609',
    success: '#12BF26',
    disable: '#DFDFDF',
  },
  lines: {
    gray: '#DFDFDF',
    accent: '#B0C2FF',
  },
  background: {
    light: '#FFFFFF',
    'accent-light': '#DCE7FF',
  },
}
```

**Usage Pattern:**
- Use Tailwind classes: `bg-basic-accent`, `text-text-dark`, `border-lines-gray`
- Aliases available: `text-basic-gray`, `bg-basic-secondary`, etc.
- State colors: `bg-states-error`, `text-states-success`

### Typography Tokens

Font families:
- `font-jersey` - Jersey 10 (for logo/branding)
- `font-inter` - Inter (primary UI font)
- `font-istok-web` - Istok Web (headings)

Font sizes (defined in `tailwind.config.js`):
```javascript
fontSize: {
  'heading-40': ['40px', { lineHeight: '100%', fontWeight: '700' }],
  'heading-32': ['32px', { lineHeight: '100%', fontWeight: '700' }],
  'medium-24': ['24px', { lineHeight: '100%', fontWeight: '500' }],
  'regular-24': ['24px', { lineHeight: '100%', fontWeight: '400' }],
  'regular-20': ['20px', { lineHeight: '100%', fontWeight: '400' }],
  'regular-16': ['16px', { lineHeight: '100%', fontWeight: '400' }],
  'light-16': ['16px', { lineHeight: '100%', fontWeight: '300' }],
}
```

**Usage:**
```tsx
<h1 className="font-istok-web font-bold text-heading-32 text-text-dark">
  Title
</h1>
<p className="font-inter font-normal text-regular-24 text-text-dark">
  Body text
</p>
```

### Spacing Tokens

Custom spacing values:
```javascript
spacing: {
  'header-content': '92px',    // Header to content gap
  'title-subtitle': '52px',     // Title to subtitle gap
  'title-rows': '32px',         // Title to rows gap
  'table-rows': '20px',         // Table row spacing
  'title-description': '4px',   // Title to description gap
  'breadcrumbs-title': '12px', // Breadcrumbs to title gap
}
```

**Usage:**
- Use Tailwind spacing: `gap-[40px]`, `px-[120px]`, `py-[40px]`
- Custom spacing: `pt-[92px]` for header-content spacing

## 2. Component Library

### Location
- **UI Components**: `web/src/components/ui/`
- **Domain Components**: `web/src/components/domain/`
- **Layout**: `web/src/components/Layout.tsx`

### Component Architecture

Components are functional React components with TypeScript:

```tsx
// Example pattern from Button.tsx
import React from "react";
import clsx from "clsx";

export type ButtonVariant = "primary" | "secondary" | "danger" | ...;
export type ButtonSize = "big-text" | "small-text" | "small-icon" | ...;

interface ButtonProps extends React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement> {
  variant?: ButtonVariant;
  size?: ButtonSize;
  icon?: React.ReactNode;
  fullWidth?: boolean;
}

export const Button: React.FC<ButtonProps> = ({
  variant = "primary",
  size = "big-text",
  icon,
  children,
  className,
  ...rest
}) => {
  return (
    <button
      className={clsx(
        "inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-[10px] rounded-[4px]",
        getVariantClasses(variant, state),
        getSizeClasses(size),
        className
      )}
      {...rest}
    >
      {icon && <span className="flex-shrink-0">{icon}</span>}
      {children}
    </button>
  );
};
```

### Key Patterns

1. **Type Safety**: All components use TypeScript with exported types
2. **Composition**: Components accept `className` and spread `...rest` props
3. **Styling**: Use `clsx` for conditional class names
4. **Icons**: Icons passed as `React.ReactNode` via `icon` prop or `children`

### Available UI Components

- `Button` - Multiple variants and sizes
- `Input` - Text input with states (default, focus, error, success, disabled)
- `TextArea` - Multi-line text input
- `Select` - Dropdown select
- `Avatar` - User avatar with initials
- `Breadcrumbs` - Navigation breadcrumbs
- `Modal` - Modal dialog
- `Toast` - Toast notifications
- `ConfirmDialog` - Confirmation dialog
- `EmptyState` - Empty state display
- `Badge` - Badge component
- `Toggle` - Toggle switch
- `Table` - Table component
- `FormField` - Form field wrapper

## 3. Frameworks & Libraries

### Core Stack
- **Framework**: React 19.1.1
- **Language**: TypeScript 5.9.3
- **Routing**: React Router DOM 7.9.5
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4.1.16
- **Build Tool**: Vite 7.1.7
- **Utility**: clsx 2.1.0 (for conditional classes)

### Styling Approach

**Tailwind CSS v4** with:
- PostCSS (`@tailwindcss/postcss`)
- Custom theme extensions
- Utility classes in `@layer utilities`

**Pattern:**
```tsx
// Use Tailwind utility classes
<div className="flex items-center justify-between gap-[24px] px-[120px] py-[40px]">
  <span className="font-inter font-normal text-regular-24 text-text-dark">
    Content
  </span>
</div>
```

**No CSS Modules or Styled Components** - all styling via Tailwind classes.

## 4. Asset Management

### Location
- **Static Assets**: `web/public/`
- **Source Assets**: `web/src/assets/`
- **Build Output**: `web/dist/`

### Asset Patterns
- Images: Place in `public/` for direct access or `src/assets/` for imports
- Icons: SVG components in `web/src/components/ui/Icons.tsx` or `EyeIcon.tsx`
- No CDN configuration currently

## 5. Icon System

### Location
- **Main Icons**: `web/src/components/ui/Icons.tsx`
- **Special Icons**: `web/src/components/ui/EyeIcon.tsx`

### Icon Pattern

Icons are React components returning SVG:

```tsx
export const TrashIcon: React.FC<{ className?: string }> = ({ 
  className = "" 
}) => {
  return (
    <svg
      className={className}
      width="24"
      height="24"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
    >
      <path
        d="M3 6h18..."
        stroke="currentColor"
        strokeWidth="2"
        strokeLinecap="round"
        strokeLinejoin="round"
      />
    </svg>
  );
};
```

### Available Icons
- `EyeIcon` - Eye (open/closed) with `open` prop
- `ExitIcon` - Exit/logout
- `TrashIcon` - Delete/trash
- `EditIcon` - Edit/pencil
- `CheckIcon` - Checkmark
- `CopyIcon` - Copy
- `CrossIcon` - Close/X
- `DiceIcon` - Dice/random

### Usage
```tsx
import { TrashIcon } from '../components/ui/Icons';

<Button>
  <TrashIcon className="size-6" />
</Button>
```

**Naming Convention**: PascalCase with `Icon` suffix (e.g., `TrashIcon`, `EditIcon`)

## 6. Styling Approach

### CSS Methodology
- **Utility-First**: Tailwind CSS utility classes
- **No CSS Modules**: All styles via Tailwind
- **No Styled Components**: Functional components with className
- **Global Styles**: `web/src/index.css` for base styles and utilities

### Global Styles
Located in `web/src/index.css`:
- Base body styles
- Custom utility classes via `@layer utilities`
- Keyframe animations (e.g., `slide-in`)

### Responsive Design
- Tailwind responsive prefixes: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`, `2xl:`
- Fixed breakpoints (not customized in config)
- Mobile-first approach

### State Management
- Component-level state with React hooks
- Context API for global state (`AuthContext`, `ToastContext`)
- No Redux or other state management library

## 7. Project Structure

```
web/
├── src/
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── ui/              # Reusable UI components
│   │   ├── domain/          # Domain-specific components
│   │   └── Layout.tsx       # Main layout component
│   ├── pages/               # Page components (routes)
│   ├── contexts/            # React contexts
│   ├── services/            # API services
│   ├── utils/               # Utility functions
│   ├── assets/              # Source assets
│   ├── index.css            # Global styles
│   ├── main.tsx             # Entry point
│   └── App.tsx              # Root component
├── public/                  # Static assets
